{"title":"Longest Palindromic Subsequence","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Given a string `s` of lowercase English letters, find the length of its **longest palindromic subsequence**.\n\nA subsequence is obtained by deleting zero or more characters from `s` without changing the order of the remaining characters (the kept characters do not have to be adjacent, unlike a substring). A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards. A single character is a palindrome, so the answer is always at least `1`.\n\n**Follow-up:** a variant asks the same question for a sequence of airport codes written as one hyphen-separated string, for example `DEL-BOM-BLR-BOM-DEL`: find the longest palindromic subsequence of **codes**, treating each whole code as one symbol. Be ready to adapt your solution to it.","inputFormat":"A single line containing the string `s`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of `s`.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s| ≤ 1500","`s` consists of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"character","output":"5","explanation":"Keep c, a, r, a, c (positions 0, 2, 3, 4, 5) to get `carac`, which reads the same in both directions. No palindromic subsequence of length 6 exists."},{"input":"abcd","output":"1","explanation":"All letters are different, so the best palindrome is a single character."},{"input":"agbdba","output":"5","explanation":"Deleting the `g` leaves `abdba`, a palindrome of length 5. The whole string `agbdba` is not a palindrome."}],"tests":[{"input":"a","output":"1"},{"input":"ab","output":"1"},{"input":"aa","output":"2"},{"input":"abc","output":"1"},{"input":"aba","output":"3"},{"input":"abca","output":"3"},{"input":"aabaa","output":"5"},{"input":"abcdefg","output":"1"},{"input":"zzzzzzzz","output":"8"},{"input":"abcba","output":"5"},{"input":"abcdcbaefg","output":"7"},{"input":"xukgpbuzpcebk","output":"5"},{"input":"aabacaccc","output":"5"},{"input":"aaaa","output":"4"},{"input":"ddcbfdffacba","output":"5"},{"input":"ababbabaaaba","output":"9"},{"input":"baab","output":"4"},{"input":"tevfmmgxu","output":"2"},{"input":"","output":"477"},{"input":"","output":"1221"},{"input":"","output":"1500"},{"input":"","output":"1374"}],"complexity":{"time":"O(n^2)","space":"O(n)"},"hints":["Let f(i, j) be the answer for the substring s[i..j]. Think about what happens when s[i] == s[j] and when they differ.","If s[i] == s[j] then f(i, j) = f(i + 1, j - 1) + 2; otherwise f(i, j) = max(f(i + 1, j), f(i, j - 1)). A single character gives f(i, i) = 1.","Fill the table with i decreasing and j increasing, keeping only the previous row, or note that the answer equals the longest common subsequence of s and its reverse."],"starters":{"python":"import sys\n\n\ndef longest_palindromic_subsequence(s: str) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here\n    return 0\n\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().split()[0]\n    print(longest_palindromic_subsequence(s))\n\n\nmain()\n","javascript":"function longestPalindromicSubsequence(s) {\n  // Write your solution here\n  return 0\n}\n\nconst s = input.trim().split(/\\s+/)[0]\nconsole.log(String(longestPalindromicSubsequence(s)))\n","cpp":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint longestPalindromicSubsequence(const string& s) {\n    // Write your solution here\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    cout << longestPalindromicSubsequence(s) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static int longestPalindromicSubsequence(String s) {\n        // Write your solution here\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String s = br.readLine().trim();\n        System.out.println(longestPalindromicSubsequence(s));\n    }\n}\n"},"reconstructed":false}